-- title:
--   Residue field of Specℤ at (ℓ) as quotient of ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime number, let $s$ be a point of the scheme $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}$, and assume that the prime ideal of $\mathbf{Z}$ corresponding to $s$ is the ideal generated by $\ell$. Write $R =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) for the subring of $\mathbf{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$ (i.e. $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$ realised inside $\mathbf{Q}$). The assertion is that there exists a ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon R \to \kappa(s)$ into the residue field of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}$ at $s$ (the residue field of the local ring of the scheme at $s$) such that: $\varphi$ is surjective; $\varphi$ sends the element $\ell$ of $R$ to $0$; and the composite of $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi \colon \operatorname{Spec}\kappa(s) \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ followed by the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}$ induced by the structure map $\mathbf{Z} \to R$ is equal to the canonical morphism $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa(s) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}$ given by `fromSpecResidueField s`.
--
--   This identifies $\kappa(s) \cong \mathbf{F}_\ell$ as a quotient of $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$ by reduction modulo $\ell$, compatibly with the canonical morphism from the residue field spectrum at $s$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}$; surjectivity together with $\varphi(\ell)=0$ expresses that $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ hits the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$. It serves as a base-change device in the study of multiplication-by-$n$ on Jacobians with good reduction, where it is used to pass from $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$ to the characteristic-$\ell$ fibre.
-- source:
